From dc1f36a75a77095799e2434caae2c804bc216c83 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Alexandre Daubois <alex.daubois@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 14 Sep 2026 09:12:03 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 10/20] Fix GHSA-fpwc-w8rq-cr92: strip credentials from user
 headers on cross-origin redirects

Authorization, Cookie and Proxy-Authorization set through the http context
were forwarded verbatim when follow_location sent the request to another
origin. They are now stripped from the user header bag whenever the
redirect target differs in scheme, host or port, including when the header
name is repeated or the bag uses malformed line endings.

